  "title": "How Fabric Data Agents Are Powering the Next Wave of AI | BRK1739",
  "description": "Unlock the next level of enterprise AI with Fabric data agents\u2014now featuring integration with M365 Copilot, managed MCP server endpoints, and reasoning across structured and unstructured data in OneLake. Learn how these innovations empower your teams to unify data sources and deploy intelligent, interoperable AI solutions faster and more securely. With MCP support, Fabric data agents can streamline governance and connectivity across the enterprise, enabling data-driven decision-making at scale.\n\nTo learn more, please check out these resources:\nhttps://aka.ms/ignite25-plans-agentic...\n\n\n\ud835\udde6\ud835\uddfd\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddee\ud835\uddf8\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddff\ud835\ude00:\nShreyas Canchi Radhakrishna\nAmir Jafari\n\n\n\ud835\udde6\ud835\uddf2\ud835\ude00\ud835\ude00\ud835\uddf6\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddfb \ud835\udddc\ud835\uddfb\ud835\uddf3\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddff\ud835\uddfa\ud835\uddee\ud835\ude01\ud835\uddf6\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddfb:\nThis is one of many sessions from the Microsoft Ignite 2025 event. View even more sessions on-demand and learn about Microsoft Ignite at https://ignite.microsoft.com\n\nBRK1739 | English (US) | Unify your data platform, Microsoft Fabric\n\n\nBreakout | Intermediate (200)\n\n\n#MSIgnite, #Unifyyourdataplatform\n\nChapters:\n0:00 - Overview of Microsoft Fabric as a Unified Data Platform\n00:02:06 - Capabilities and Connectivity of Fabric Data Agents\n00:12:07 - Generating CSV reports in VS Code using Fabric Data Agent\n00:22:42 - Introduction to new Data Agent experiences\n00:26:14 - Defining agent instructions and demonstrating query execution\n00:29:02 - Ontology integration and reasoning over semantic relationships\n00:34:47 - Introducing Data Agent Setup and Markdown Editor\n00:42:24 - Audience Q&A on Ontology, Semantic Models, and Unstructured Data\n00:43:42 - Clarification on Data Agent Studio and Multi-Agent Capabilities",
